From 7ea30c8345a596c0f9637bdc3468f2b7c4d6997e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:30:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] grate: leave SFU results, fetch results and SFU operands in
 place

The fragment compiler copied every value into a register of its own:
24 of the 77 slot ops of the glmark2 bump-height shader were plain
copies, NVIDIA's compiler has one. Consume a value where it is
produced instead, like NVIDIA does:

- An SFU result of one channel (no saturate) stays in the SFU's row
  register, the next instruction reads it there. The allocator looks
  for a row for it (sfu_result_in_row), and avoid_rows no longer
  counts an SFU op's own result as a value that lives across the op.
- A fetch result stays in the R2/R3 half it lands in when nothing
  overwrites it while it is wanted: a coordinate that dies in the
  fetch frees its row for the result, the sequential lane check is
  skipped for a fetch, and the row safety scan ends where the channel
  is redefined (it used to count the new value). No copy is emitted
  for such a channel.
- The SFU operand is written by its producer step directly into the
  SFU row (retarget_sfu_operand), or is already there; no load step.
  This drops the |x| the load applied to RSQ, like NVIDIA, whose sum
  goes straight into the SFU register (inversesqrt of a negative
  value is undefined in GLSL).
- Earlier in the series of this change: forward_tex_coord folds
  MOV t.xy, s.xy; TEX t, t.xy for temporaries, emit_TEX skips result
  channels that are never read, retarget_coord_producer lets the step
  before a fetch write R0/R1, and sink_coord_producers moves a
  coordinate producer down to its fetch.

Bump height: 77 ops / 41 packets / 24 copies before, 54 / 32 / 13 now
(NVIDIA: 40 real ops, 13 packets).

Checked on the tablet: run-grate-tests.sh has the same pass and fail
lines as the library without this change (including grate-pow-test
21/21, grate-frag-compare-test, grate-blend-test and
grate-texture-multi-fetch-test); glmark2 bump height and
blinn-phong-inf render without errors, 52 and 46-47 FPS (45 before).
Not yet compared against a fresh cgtest compile.
